\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Sources for two-valued signs}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{For a translation-invariant real Majorana chain, Kitaev factors the total Pfaffian into contributions of self-opposite momenta and determinants from conjugate pairs \citet{v2, Eqs. (23)–(26), printed pp. 11–12}{kitaev2001unpaired}. In his Fourier convention these determinants are positive: the spectrum of the Hermitian multiple of a Fourier block stays gapped on the whole momentum circle and has equal positive and negative dimensions. The finite rotation plane in \ref{fdip-01AS} has just two nonreal labels and has no such family supplied.}

\p{Fu and Kane express parity indices as products of inversion eigenvalues at invariant momenta, taking one from each occupied Kramers pair \citet{v2, Eqs. (1.1)–(1.2), p. 2; (3.5)–(3.10), p. 9}{fu2007topological}. Their argument uses a smooth choice of gauge. The eigenpair statement of \ref{fdip-01AX} uses only the finite negative spaces. Schnyder, Ryu, Furusaki and Ludwig list the 10 single-particle symmetry classes and their symmetry signs \citet{v3, Table I, printed p. 2}{schnyder2008classification}.}
